{
  "example": "A helper function inside `mod tests` has no reference and is read by no record.\n`habeas status --coverage` does not warn about it. A `#[test]` function in the\nsame module without a `{test}` reference is still a validation error.\n{test}`requirements.references.coverage.report`\n{test}`requirements.references.coverage.tests`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example describes a concrete case with two expected outcomes. (1) An unreferenced helper in `mod tests` that no record reads draws no coverage warning. (2) A `#[test]` function in the same module with no `{test}` reference is still a validation error.\n\nThe tests cover both outcomes:\n\n- `tests/coverage.rs#fn[a_test_without_a_test_reference_fails_validation_even_in_mod_tests]` builds `src/lib.rs` with `fn parse`, plus `mod tests` holding a helper `fixture` and a `#[test] fn checks`.\n  - It asserts that validation errors include the exact \"test function checks has no {test} reference\" message, with a path and line prefix. This covers outcome 2.\n  - It asserts that no error mentions `fixture`.\n  - It asserts that `warned(root)` equals `[\"parse\"]`, so the `mod tests` helper is not warned about. `warned` wraps `habeas::coverage_warnings`, the library function behind `status --coverage`. This covers outcome 1.\n- `tests/coverage.rs#fn[coverage_lasts_for_three_reauthorings_of_the_record_that_read_an_item]` uses the `project()` fixture, which contains `fixture` inside `mod tests`. At every stage, including the stage where `parse` becomes warned, `warned` lists only `parse` and `helper` and never `fixture`. This shows the exclusion persists across the history scenario.\n- `tests/coverage.rs#fn[items_in_out_of_line_tests_modules_are_not_warned_about]` and `src/coverage_history.rs#mod[tests]/fn[files_declared_as_tests_modules_are_in_a_tests_module]` extend the same behavior to `tests.rs` and `tests/` files. Positive and negative path cases include `src/tests.rs`, `src/foo/tests/mod.rs`, `src/foo.rs` and `tests/tests.rs`.\n\nThe assertions derive from the example text, and the positive and negative cases are both exercised. I found no gap.",
